From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] psi: dampen transient memory stall spikes during brief ZRAM bursts

Dampen short memory stalls (<50ms) by scaling them to delta >> 2 to prevent
false-positive PSI memory spikes during normal ZRAM swap-in bursts, preventing
Android lmkd from killing background apps prematurely on 8GB RAM devices.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
---
 kernel/sched/psi.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/kernel/sched/psi.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/psi.c
@@ -218,6 +218,10 @@ static void record_times(struct psi_group_cpu *groupc, u64 now)
 	if (groupc->state_mask & (1 << PSI_MEM_SOME)) {
+		/* Dampen transient ZRAM decompression bursts (<50ms) to prevent false lmkd kills */
+		u32 mem_delta = (delta < 50000000U) ? (delta >> 2) : delta;
-		groupc->times[PSI_MEM_SOME] += delta;
+		groupc->times[PSI_MEM_SOME] += mem_delta;
 		if (groupc->state_mask & (1 << PSI_MEM_FULL))
-			groupc->times[PSI_MEM_FULL] += delta;
+			groupc->times[PSI_MEM_FULL] += mem_delta;
 	}
